{\pard\qc\sb400\sa200{\f0\fs52\b\cf2 URBAN PL}\par}
{\pard\qc\sa100{\f0\fs24\cf3 Business Plan  |  Confidential  |  May 2026}\par}
{\pard\qc\sa400{\f0\fs20\cf3 urbanpleague  |  admin@theurbanpl.com  |  www.theurbanpl.com}\par}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 1. Executive Summary}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Urban PL is a competitive pickup soccer platform that brings real league structure to casual football. Players join organized games through the app, pay a \$16.99 entry fee, and compete in refereed, stat-tracked matches that feed into a city-wide rankings system.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 The platform operates on an asset-light model \'96 no fields owned, no full-time staff. Referees are matched to games like Uber matches drivers to rides, funded directly from player entry fees. Stats collected by referees build player ratings, which power balanced lineups and a virtual league ecosystem that keeps players coming back week after week.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Urban PL launches Summer 2026 across three South Florida cities \'96 Boca Raton, Fort Lauderdale, and West Palm Beach \'96 starting with an inaugural tournament in each city followed by recurring weekly games.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 2. The Problem}\par}
{\pard\sa160{\f0\fs22\b No competitive structure.}{\f0\fs22  Games organized through WhatsApp groups or apps like Meetup or Plei lack any system for tracking wins, goals, or player performance. There\'92s nothing at stake and nothing to play for beyond the game itself.\par}}
{\pard\sa160{\f0\fs22\b No referee.}{\f0\fs22  Without a neutral official, disputed calls turn fun games into arguments. Players quit. Games fall apart. There\'92s no accountability.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22\b Unbalanced teams.}{\f0\fs22  When skill levels are mixed and team selection is informal \'96 friends picking friends \'96 one side dominates and the game stops being fun. Nobody comes back.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 3. The Solution}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Urban PL organizes pickup soccer through a two-sided platform: a player app and a referee portal.\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa100{\f0\fs22 \'95  Players browse available games, pay a \$16.99 entry fee, and show up\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa100{\f0\fs22 \'95  A verified referee is assigned to every game, funded from the entry fees collected\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa100{\f0\fs22 \'95  The referee tracks live stats: goals, assists, yellow/red cards, results\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa100{\f0\fs22 \'95  Stats are converted into player ratings\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa100{\f0\fs22 \'95  Ratings power a snake-draft lineup algorithm that balances teams before every game\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa200{\f0\fs22 \'95  Cumulative stats feed a city rankings leaderboard \'96 a virtual league that rewards consistency and performance\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 4. Target Audience}\par}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Competitive seekers:}{\f0\fs22  Players who want stats, rankings, and fair competition\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Soccer social seekers:}{\f0\fs22  Players looking for a community and regular games\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Urban culture seekers:}{\f0\fs22  Young adults drawn to the identity and lifestyle around the game\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22\b Convenience seekers:}{\f0\fs22  Players who want to show up and play without organizing anything\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Core demographic: Men 18\'9635, urban, soccer-active, South Florida.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 5. Market Opportunity}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Over 30 million Americans play soccer recreationally. The 18\'9635 urban demographic is underserved \'96 organized leagues require seasonal commitment, and pickup apps offer convenience but no competitive structure. Urban PL sits in the gap: self-serve like pickup, structured like a league.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 South Florida is the ideal launch market \'96 large Latino and soccer-forward population, year-round outdoor play, and no dominant platform in the organized competitive pickup space.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 6. Competitive Landscape}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22\b Plei}{\f0\fs22  is the most direct competitor \'96 strong in South Florida, good UX, but no referee system, no stat tracking, and no real competitive structure. They charge \$12\'9618 per game. Urban PL undercuts that price at \$16.99 while delivering a significantly better product: a referee included, balanced teams, live stats, and a rankings system.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b WhatsApp / Meetup:}{\f0\fs22  No structure, no referee, no stats. The real \'93competition\'94 is chaos.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22\b ZogSports / Rec Leagues:}{\f0\fs22  Fixed seasons, team registration required, no referee matching or player ratings. Not self-serve.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Plei owns the convenience seeker. Urban PL targets everyone who wants the game to actually mean something. They can co-exist \'96 Plei brings people into organized pickup, Urban PL is where competitive players migrate.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 7. Business Model}\par}

{\pard\sb200\sa120{\f0\fs26\b Phase 1 \'96 Entry Fees (Launch, Month 1\'966)}\par}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22 Entry fee: \$16.99 per player per game (7v7, 1 hour)\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Field rental (1hr avg):  \$160\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Referee (1hr @ \$45):      \$45\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  AI Camera (monthly \'f7 4 games): \$9\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Total cost per game:       \$214\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Revenue (14 x \$16.99):     \$237.86\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa200{\f0\fs22\b \'95  Net margin per game:       \$23.86\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Tournament pricing: \$25\'9628 per player. Revenue per tournament (65 players avg @ \$26): \$1,690. Costs: ~\$350. Margin: ~\$1,340.\par}}

{\pard\sb200\sa120{\f0\fs26\b Phase 2 \'96 Memberships (Month 6+)}\par}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Drop-in: \$16.99/game \'96 Standard access\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Member: \$55/month \'96 4 guaranteed weekly spots + priority registration\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa200{\f0\fs22 \'95  Pro: \$89/month \'96 Membership + AI highlight clips\par}}

{\pard\sb200\sa120{\f0\fs26\b Phase 3 \'96 AI Video Highlights (Month 9+)}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 AI camera hardware: \$99 one-time lease + \$35/month per field. Automatically records and clips player highlights. Sold as a premium add-on or included in Pro membership.\par}}

{\pard\sb200\sa120{\f0\fs26\b Phase 4 \'96 Sponsorships}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Soccer gear brands, sports drink companies, and local soccer-social venues sponsor games, tournaments, and city rankings.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 8. Launch Plan}\par}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Month 1 \'96 Boca Raton:}{\f0\fs22  Tournament #1 (60\'9670 players). Weekly games start the following week.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Month 2 \'96 Fort Lauderdale:}{\f0\fs22  Tournament #2 (60\'9670 players). Weekly games start the following week.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22\b Month 3 \'96 West Palm Beach:}{\f0\fs22  Tournament #3 (60\'9670 players). Weekly games start the following week.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 By end of Month 3: three cities running concurrent weekly games with an established rated player base in each.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22\b The flywheel:}{\f0\fs22  Tournament acquires players \'96\'96 weekly games retain them \'96\'96 stats build ratings \'96\'96 ratings hook competitive players \'96\'96 word of mouth grows the next city.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 9. Player Recruitment}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Each tournament targets 60\'9670 players and serves as a high-energy introduction to the platform. One great first experience converts casual players into weekly regulars.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Instagram (@urbanpleague):}{\f0\fs22  Match day content, goal clips, rankings highlights, player spotlights. The most important channel for this demographic.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Flyers & field presence:}{\f0\fs22  Target existing soccer fields, futsal courts, and sports stores in each city 2\'963 weeks before each tournament.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Referral program:}{\f0\fs22  Players who bring a friend to their first game receive credit toward a future game.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Targeted Meta ads:}{\f0\fs22  Soccer interest + South Florida geo + 18\'9635 age, running 3 weeks before each tournament.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Local soccer groups:}{\f0\fs22  Facebook groups, WhatsApp communities, and local leagues where players are already organized but frustrated with the informal structure.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22\b Plei spillover:}{\f0\fs22  Players who\'92ve tried Plei but want more. The \$16.99 price point makes switching an easy decision.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Target: 40\'9650 registered app users per city before Tournament Day.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 10. Referee Recruitment}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Referees are the backbone of the platform. Quality referees directly determine the player experience.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Who to recruit:}{\f0\fs22  USSF-certified referees, college soccer players and coaches, retired or semi-retired players, and local referee association members.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b How to recruit:}{\f0\fs22  Instagram and local soccer Facebook groups, flyers at university athletic departments, direct outreach to the USSF South Florida chapter, and the in-app referee sign-up portal with ID verification.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Retention incentives:}{\f0\fs22  \$50 bonus after 5 completed games, consistent weekly schedule, performance ratings that build referee reputation in-app, and priority assignment to tournaments for top-rated officials.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Target: 6\'968 verified referees across South Florida before Month 1 tournament.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 11. Retention Strategy}\par}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Target retention rates:}\par}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Tournament \'96\'96 first weekly game conversion: 50\'9660%\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Month 1 \'96\'96 Month 2 retention: 55\'9665%\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Month 3 established weekly player: 70%+\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa200{\f0\fs22 \'95  6-month active player retention: 50%+\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f0\fs22 Recreational sports apps average 25\'9635% monthly retention. Urban PL\'92s competitive hooks \'96 ratings, rankings, and the drive to improve your standing \'96 are specifically designed to beat that average.\par}}
{\pard\sa100{\f0\fs22\b Retention tactics:}\par}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Rankings: players with something to protect come back every week\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Push notifications: game day reminders, lineup reveal, weekly rankings updates\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  SMS reminders: team assignment and kickoff reminder before every game\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Match reports: shareable results with goals, cards, and stats\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Season arcs: quarterly resets with trophies for top finishers\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Streaks: reward players who play every week with a visible profile streak\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa200{\f0\fs22 \'95  Waitlist friction: full games create FOMO and drive early registration next time\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

{\pard\sb400\sa160{\f0\fs32\b 12. Operations}\par}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Fields: Rented per game from existing venues. No ownership required.\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Referees: Recruited, verified (ID + age check), and player-rated in-app. Paid per game.\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  AI Cameras: \$99 one-time lease + \$35/month per field. No operator required.\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa80{\f0\fs22 \'95  Admin: Full in-app admin panel for game creation, payments, referee assignments, and payouts.\par}}
{\pard\li400\sa200{\f0\fs22 \'95  Tech: iOS (App Store). React Native + Supabase. Push notifications, SMS, Stripe payments.\par}}

\pard\sb300\sa100\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrsp100 \par

